'''Portuguese''' (''português'') is a Romance language spoken by about 250 million people in [[Portugal]], [[Brazil]], [[Angola]] and other countries.<ref>A reference that the pack leaves out.</ref>

This phrasebook uses European Portuguese; Brazilian differences are noted.

==Pronunciation guide==
===Vowels===
; a : like 'a' in "father"
; e : like 'e' in "bet"

===Consonants===
; ç : like 's' in "sun"
; lh : like 'lli' in "million"

==Phrase list==
===Basics===
{{Phrasebookguide}}
<!-- The basic phrases. -->
; Hello. : Olá. (''oh-LAH'')
; Hello. ''(informal)'' : Oi. (''oy'')
; How are you? : Como está? (''KOH-moo ish-TAH?'')
; Fine, thank you. : Bem, obrigado (male) / obrigada (female). (''bayñ, oh-bree-GAH-doo / oh-bree-GAH-dah'')
; What is your name?
: Como se chama? (''KOH-moo seh SHAH-mah?'')
; My name is ______ . : Chamo-me ______ . (''SHAH-moo meh _____ .'')
; Please. : Por favor. (''poor fah-VOHR'')
; Thank you. : Obrigado. (''oh-bree-GAH-doo'')
; Yes. : Sim. (''seeng'')
; No. : Não. (''nowng'')
; Excuse me. (''getting attention'') : Com licença. (''kohng lee-SEHN-sah'')
; I don't understand. : Não compreendo. (''nowng kohm-pree-EHN-doo'')
; Where is the toilet? : Onde é a casa de banho? (''OHN-deh eh ah KAH-zah deh BAH-nyoo?'')
; Hello. : Olá. (''oh-LAH'')

====Problems====
; Leave me alone. : Deixe-me em paz. (''DAY-sheh meh ayñ pahsh'')
; Help! : Socorro! (''soo-KOH-hoo!'')
; Call the [[police]]! : Chame a polícia! (''SHAH-meh ah poo-LEE-see-ah!'')
; I'm lost. : Estou perdido. (''ish-TOH pehr-DEE-doo'')

===Numbers===
; 1 : um (''oong'')
; 2 : dois (''doysh'')
; 3 : três (''traysh'')
; 10 : dez (''dehsh'')
; 100 : cem (''sayñ'')

===Time===
; now : agora (''ah-GOH-rah'')
; later : mais tarde (''mysh TAHR-deh'')
; morning : manhã (''mah-NYAHN'')

====Clock time====
; one o'clock AM : uma da manhã (''OO-mah dah mah-NYAHN'')
; It's 10:30. : São dez e meia. (''sowng dehsh ee MAY-ah'')

===Transportation===
====Directions====
; How do I get to the train station? : Como chego à estação de comboios? (''KOH-moo SHEH-goo ah ish-tah-SOWNG deh kohm-BOY-oosh?'')
; left : esquerda (''ish-KEHR-dah'')
; right : direita (''dee-RAY-tah'')
* straight ahead : em frente (''ayñ FREHN-teh'')
{{phrasebook|north|norte|NOHR-teh}}

===Eating===
; A table for one person, please. : Uma mesa para uma pessoa, por favor. (''OO-mah MEH-zah PAH-rah OO-mah peh-SOH-ah, poor fah-VOHR'')
; The check, please. : A conta, por favor. (''ah KOHN-tah, poor fah-VOHR'')
; water : água (''AH-gwah'')
; coffee : café (''kah-FEH'')
; I'm a vegetarian. : Sou vegetariano/vegetariana. (''soh veh-zheh-tah-ree-AH-noo'')

===Bars===
; A beer, please. : Uma cerveja, por favor. (''OO-mah sehr-VAY-zhah, poor fah-VOHR'')
; Cheers! : Saúde! (''sah-OO-deh'')

